        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Concussion Note", "A concussion diagnosis.")],
        role: "EMT partner",
        exam: [.direct("Describe your role and what happened for the jury.", "\"I'm {V}'s partner on the ambulance. We responded to a one-car crash at about ten at night, and {D} was the driver.\""), .direct("What happened during the roadside care?", "\"{D} kicked {V}, a firefighter-EMT, in the thigh as we were treating {D} after a crash. The dash camera recorded it.\""), .direct("What was {V}'s injury?", "\"A bruised thigh, as the medical note records. {V} stayed on the call and finished treating {D}.\""), .direct("What did you see {D} do before the kick?", "\"{D} lashed out. {D} was agitated and swinging an arm, and then the kick landed on {V}.\""), .direct("How did {D} act when you reached the car?", "\"{D} was agitated and swinging an arm. {D} didn't answer questions and tried to get out of the car.\""), .direct("What did you do after {D} kicked you?", "\"I stepped back, called for backup and kept {D} from standing. My partner took over care while I checked my leg.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} was dazed after the crash, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. An ER nurse says {D} had a concussion. I will agree it was a bad crash.\""), .cross("Had {D} been drinking?", "\"I smelled alcohol. I cannot say how much {D} had had.\""), .cross("Was {D} cooperative afterward?", "\"{D} calmed down after a few minutes. {D} apologized later.\""), .cross("Did {D} seem to know what was happening?", "\"Not really. {D} seemed confused and kept asking where {D.he} was.\""), .cross("{D} was bleeding from the head and confused when you arrived, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. There was a cut over {D.his} eye and {D.he} was slow to answer. That is why we began care at the roadside.\"")],
        defenseRole: "ER nurse",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Tell the jury about your work and your exam of {D}.", "\"I'm an emergency room nurse. I examined {D} after the ambulance brought {D} in.\""), .direct("Did {D} have a concussion when you treated {D.him}?", "\"Yes. The scan and the exam both showed a concussion. {D} was confused and could not follow simple questions.\""), .direct("How severe was the concussion?", "\"Moderate. {D} was dazed and slow to respond, and that kind of injury can make a person lash out.\""), .direct("Can a concussion cause a patient to kick or swing at people?", "\"Yes. Patients can be confused and combative without meaning to be. We see it often in the ER.\""), .direct("What did your exam show?", "\"A concussion, confirmed by a scan. {D} was dazed and slow to respond.\""), .direct("Can a concussion cause a patient to lash out?", "\"Yes. Confused patients can swing or kick without meaning to or remembering it afterward.\""), .cross("Had {D} also been drinking before the crash?", "\"I smelled alcohol. A blood test showed a reading, and that can add to confusion too.\""), .cross("Would a concussion excuse a kick at a medic?", "\"It explains it, but it does not excuse it. I would not say it is the same as intent.\""), .cross("Did {D} remember the kick afterward?", "\"No. {D} did not remember it. {D} was told about it later.\""), .cross("Had {D} been drinking?", "\"I smelled alcohol, and a blood test showed a level. I can't say how it affected the concussion.\""), .cross("A concussion does not always cause someone to lash out, does it?", "\"No. It varies a great deal. Some patients are quiet, others are agitated, and I cannot say how it would affect any one person.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} kicked an EMT.", "A concussion."),
        allocution: "\"I should have walked away.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been drinking.", "The ER confirmed a concussion."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you kick {V}?", "\"I do not remember it, but I am told I did. I had just been in a crash, and I was dazed.\""), .direct("What do you remember of the roadside?", "\"Flashing lights and people around me. I felt confused, and I did not know who anyone was.\""), .direct("Had you been drinking before the crash?", "\"I had a couple of drinks. I should not have been driving. I know that.\""), .direct("Describe what you remember about the crash.", "\"Headlights and a bang, and then flashing lights and people around me. I felt confused, and my head hurt.\""), .direct("What do you remember about the kick?", "\"Nothing. I'm told it's on video, and I don't dispute it.\""), .direct("What did the hospital say?", "\"That I had a concussion. I was in the ER for several hours.\""), .cross("The dash camera shows you kicking {V}, doesn't it?", "\"It does. I am not disputing the video. I did not mean to hurt someone helping me.\""), .cross("You had been drinking, hadn't you?", "\"Yes. That did not help me stay calm. I feel awful about it.\""), .cross("{V} was bruised while trying to help you. Do you regret that?", "\"Very much. I would like to apologize to {V.him} in person.\""), .cross("You'd had a couple of drinks. Isn't that why you were combative?", "\"It didn't help. I'd been drinking, and I shouldn't have been driving.\""), .cross("{V} was trying to help you. Doesn't that make this worse?", "\"Yes. I'm sorry, and I'd like to tell {V} that in person.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} kicked {V}, a firefighter-EMT, in the thigh during roadside care after a crash. The dash camera recorded the kick, and {V} had a bruised thigh.", "The defense case is that {D} had a concussion confirmed by the ER, was dazed and confused, and does not remember the kick."),
        closings: ("A kick on dash camera, a bruised thigh, and a medic who was only trying to help. {D} had been drinking before the crash.", "A concussion confirmed by the ER and a dazed patient who lashed out without knowing it. The State must prove {D} acted on purpose."),
        timeline: [(0, "10 p.m.: the crash."), (0, "10:20 p.m.: the care."), (0, "10:25 p.m.: the kick."), (0, "11 p.m.: the ER.")],
        identified: "A dash camera.",
        mood: .sympathetic,
        impact: "I had a limp for a week.",
        doctrines: ["intoxication", "lesserIncluded"])

    static let countyClerkFeesV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.countyClerkFees",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Library Fines Clerk Pocketed Cash Payments for Two Years", "Receipt Book Shows Gaps"],
        law: "embezzlement",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Embezzled $9,200 belonging to {V}, a county library, by a person in a position of trust, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A library fines clerk, {D}, pocketed cash payments totaling $9,200 over two years. Receipts skipped numbers. {DL} says the receipt book was misnumbered.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Receipt Book", "Skipped numbers on {D}'s shifts."), E(.video, 2, "Desk Camera", "{D} pockets cash."), E(.document, 2, "Deposit Slips", "Short on those days.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Misnumbered", "{DL} says the receipt book was misnumbered.")],
        role: "Library director",
        exam: [.direct("Describe your library and how fines are collected for the jury.", "\"I direct the county library. Patrons pay fines in cash at a desk, and the clerk writes a numbered receipt and puts the money in a drawer for the day's deposit.\""), .direct("What did you find about the fines receipts?", "\"Cash fines of $9,200 over two years did not reach the deposits. The receipt book skipped numbers on {D}'s shifts.\""), .direct("What does the desk camera show?", "\"{D} pocketing cash at the desk.\""), .direct("What do the deposit slips show?", "\"They were short on those days. The shortage lines up with the skipped numbers.\""), .direct("How did you discover the problem?", "\"An audit found skipped receipt numbers on certain shifts, and the daily deposits were short by the same amounts on those days.\""), .direct("How much was missing, and over what period?", "\"About $9,200 over two years. The shortages lined up with {D}'s shifts and not with other clerks' shifts.\""), .cross("{DL} says the receipt book was misnumbered, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A misnumbered book can happen. But the deposit shortages are a separate fact.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} take the cash?", "\"I saw the camera. I wasn't at the desk.\""), .cross("Did other clerks work those shifts?", "\"Sometimes. {D}'s shifts stand out, but I can't say no one else was ever at the desk.\""), .cross("Has the receipt printer ever shipped a misnumbered book?", "\"Once, years ago. We caught it quickly, and it looked different from this pattern.\""), .cross("You did not see {D} actually take the money, did you?", "\"I saw the camera clip showing cash going into a pocket. I was not at the desk, and I cannot say what happened outside the frame.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Co-clerk",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Tell us how you know {D}.", "\"I'm a co-clerk at the same desk. We overlap on some shifts and trade off on others, and we eat lunch in the same break room.\""), .direct("Do you work with {DL}?", "\"Yes. I'm a co-clerk at the same desk.\""), .direct("Were receipts skipped?", "\"I noticed some skipped numbers. I assumed a printing issue.\""), .direct("Do you work the same shifts?", "\"Sometimes. We overlap. Other clerks work them too.\""), .direct("Did you notice skipped numbers?", "\"I noticed a few in the book from time to time. I assumed the printer had made a mistake and I didn't report it.\""), .direct("Did you handle the cash drawer?", "\"Yes, on my shifts. I closed the drawer, counted it, and signed the slip for the deposit.\""), .cross("Did you take money?", "\"No. Never. I wouldn't.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} take any?", "\"No. I never saw anything.\""), .cross("Were numbers skipped on your shifts?", "\"I don't think so, but I'm not certain. I never checked every receipt on my own shifts.\""), .cross("Did you ever see {D} take money?", "\"No. I never saw {D} take anything from the drawer, and I never saw {D} put cash in a pocket.\""), .cross("You cannot say what happened at the desk on {D}'s shifts, can you?", "\"No. I work different hours. I only know what I saw in the book, and I cannot say who handled the cash on those days.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} pocketed fines.", "A bad book."),
        allocution: "\"I knew better. I want to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} bought a motorcycle.", "The printer shipped a misnumbered book once."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why are numbers skipped?", "\"The receipt book may have been misnumbered when it arrived. I didn't notice.\""), .direct("Did you steal fines?", "\"No. I never took library money. I handled it carefully.\""), .direct("Tell us about your job at the desk.", "\"I've worked fines for six years. I take cash, write receipts, make change, and put the money in the cash drawer for the afternoon clerk.\""), .direct("Why does the camera show you with cash in your hand?", "\"I was making change and putting bills in the drawer. It looks like a pocket from that angle, but it was the drawer.\""), .direct("Do you know why numbers were skipped?", "\"The receipt book may have been misnumbered when it was printed. I filled it in order, and I didn't tear out receipts.\""), .direct("What were the skipped receipt numbers on your shifts, as you understood them?", "\"I thought it was a printer mistake. I noticed a few gaps but did not report them, because I did not want to cause trouble.\""), .cross("Receipts skipped numbers on your shifts, didn't they?", "\"That's what they say. I can't explain it.\""), .cross("Deposits were short on those days, weren't they?", "\"I didn't prepare every deposit. Others handled them.\""), .cross("The camera shows you with cash, doesn't it?", "\"It shows me handling cash. That's my job.\""), .cross("You bought a motorcycle during those two years. Where did the money come from?", "\"From savings and a loan, and a bonus from my other job. It wasn't from library fines.\""), .cross("The deposits were short on days you worked. Is that a coincidence?", "\"I didn't prepare every deposit. Others handled the drawer after me.\"")],
        openings: ("A library fines clerk, {D}, pocketed cash payments totaling $9,200 over two years. Receipts skipped numbers on {D}'s shifts, the desk camera shows {D} pocketing cash, and deposits were short. The State will present the director and the records.", "The defense will point you to a receipt book that was misnumbered, other clerks at the same desk, and a camera that shows cash handled in the ordinary way."),
        closings: ("Skipped receipt numbers on {D}'s shifts, cash going into a pocket on camera, and deposits that came up short by the same amounts. Over two years, $9,200 was gone.", "A misnumbered book and cash handled at a busy desk by several clerks. The State has not proved {D} pocketed a single dollar of library money."),
        timeline: [(-700, "Skips begin."), (0, "Year 2: audit."), (0, "Year 2: the camera."), (1, "{DL} is suspended.")],
        identified: "A receipt book.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

