        role: "Wildlife officer",
        exam: [.direct("What can you tell us about your job and the lake?", "\"I'm a wildlife officer on the lake. I investigate boating accidents, check safety equipment, and respond when something goes wrong on the water.\""), .direct("What happened on the lake after dark?", "\"A pontoon boat hit rocks, and {V}, a passenger, was killed. The operator, {D}, blew .10 on a breath test.\""), .direct("What about the boat's lights?", "\"The boat was running without lights, according to a passenger. The hull was damaged when I examined it.\""), .direct("Were the rocks marked?", "\"A channel marker had been missing for weeks. I will say that.\""), .direct("What did you find at the scene?", "\"A pontoon boat on its side against a rock outcrop. {V} had been thrown and died, and the operator was in the water holding the helm.\""), .direct("What did the breath test show?", "\"A .10 about an hour after the crash. The legal limit for operating a boat is .08.\""), .cross("{D} says the rocks were unmarked, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. A marina manager says a marker was missing for weeks and was reported.\""), .cross("Would working lights have helped {D} see the rocks?", "\"They help, though a boater still needs to watch. I cannot say it would have avoided it.\""), .cross("How fast was the boat going?", "\"Not fast, I believe. I do not have a firm number.\""), .cross("Was the channel marker missing?", "\"A marker near the rocks had been missing for weeks. I confirmed it with the marina.\""), .cross("Were the running lights required?", "\"Yes. Lights are required between sunset and sunrise, and the boat had none lit.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Marina manager",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Please describe your job at the marina.", "\"I'm the marina manager. I know the water around here, and I keep the channel markers in good order with the county.\""), .direct("Was a channel marker missing near those rocks?", "\"For weeks. The marker that warns of the rocks was gone, and boaters were relying on memory.\""), .direct("Was the missing marker reported to anyone?", "\"Yes. I reported it to the authorities more than once. Nothing was done before that night.\""), .direct("How dangerous is that stretch of water after dark?", "\"Very. Without a marker, rocks are almost impossible to see, even with lights, and many boaters use that stretch.\""), .direct("Did you report it?", "\"Yes. I reported it to the authorities more than once, in writing, and I put a notice at the dock.\""), .direct("How did you learn the marker near the rocks was missing?", "\"A fisherman told me it had been knocked down in a storm. I wrote it on my list and passed it along to the harbor office.\""), .cross("Would a sober operator have been more careful in that channel?", "\"Probably. A sober operator would be slower and watch more. I cannot say what {D} would have done.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} that evening at the marina?", "\"Yes. I saw {D} at the dock earlier. I did not see {D} drinking.\""), .cross("Does a missing marker excuse driving without running lights?", "\"No. Lights are required at night, and the marker and the lights are different safeguards.\""), .cross("Would a sober boater know about the rocks?", "\"A sober boater who knew the lake might. Someone new to the area could easily miss them.\""), .cross("A sober operator would have been more careful in that channel, wouldn't they?", "\"Yes, probably. Any operator should slow down at night and keep running lights on whether or not a marker is there.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove a boat drunk and killed a passenger.", "Unmarked rocks."),
        allocution: "\"I will never forgive myself.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been drinking for hours.", "The channel marker had been missing for weeks."),
        defendant: [.direct("Were you operating the pontoon when it hit the rocks?", "\"Yes. I was driving the boat. I did not see the rocks, and the marker that should have warned me was gone.\""), .direct("Had you been drinking before the trip?", "\"Yes. I had been drinking for hours. I should not have been behind the wheel at night.\""), .direct("Why were the running lights off?", "\"I did not turn them on. I do not remember why. It was a mistake that I regret.\""), .direct("Tell us about the ride.", "\"We took a pontoon out in the evening with a few friends. We'd been drinking for hours, and I decided to drive the boat back to the dock.\""), .direct("Why were the lights off?", "\"I didn't turn them on. I don't know why. It was getting dark, and That is on me.\""), .direct("What happened at the rocks?", "\"I didn't see them until we hit. The boat lurched and people were thrown, and I realized {V} had gone into the rocks.\""), .cross("A passenger died. Do you accept responsibility?", "\"I do. I think about {V} every day. I wish I could undo it.\""), .cross("You blame a missing marker. Is that an excuse for driving drunk without lights?", "\"No. It is not an excuse. It is part of what happened.\""), .cross("You blew a .10. Isn't that over the limit?", "\"Yes. I know what the test said, and I accept it.\""), .cross("You blame the missing marker. Isn't it your job to watch where you're going?", "\"It is. I was drinking, and I wasn't watching closely.\""), .cross("You did not turn the running lights on before you left the dock, did you?", "\"No. I forgot. We left at dusk and I assumed we would be back before dark, and I did not check the switch.\"")],
        openings: ("A pontoon boat hit unmarked rocks after dark, killing {V}, a passenger. The operator, {D}, blew .10 and was running without lights, after drinking for hours.", "The defense evidence will establish that a channel marker had been missing for weeks and was reported, and that the missing marker is part of why the boat hit the rocks."),
        closings: ("A .10 reading, no running lights, hours of drinking, and a passenger dead on the rocks. {D} was the operator of that boat, and {D} chose to go out that night.", "A channel marker missing for weeks and reported to the authorities. The State must prove {D}'s drinking, and not the missing marker, caused this death."),
